    "root/usage": "usage: aurora-render [OPTIONS] <SCENE>... [COMMAND] [-- ARGS...]",
    "root/help": "Render Aurora scenes into image files\nusage: aurora-render [OPTIONS] <SCENE>... [COMMAND] [-- ARGS...]\n\nLong description line for the root command.\n\nOptions:\n  -o, --output <FILE>       Output image path [default: out.png]\n  -w, --width <WIDTH>       Canvas width in px [range: 1, 8192] [default: 800]\n  -s, --scale <SCALE>       Scale factor [default: 1]\n  -v, --verbose             Repeat for more detail\n  -f, --force               Overwrite output\n      --dry-run             Print only\n      --margin <MARGIN>     Outer margin [default: 0]\n      --tint <TINT>         Overlay tint [default: #fff]\n      --timeout <TIMEOUT>   Give up after [default: 30s]\n      --tag <TAG> <TAG>...  Attach a tag (repeatable)\n      --format <FORMAT>     Root output format [possible values: text, json] [default: text]\n\nDiagnostics:\n      --level <LEVEL>  Log verbosity [default: info]\n      --mode <MODE>    Quality/speed trade-off [possible values: fast, balanced, quality] [default: balanced]\n\nHelp:\n  -h, --help     Show this help and exit\n  -V, --version  Show the version and exit\n\nArguments:\n  <SCENE>...  Scenes to render\n\nCommands:\n  render  Render one scene interactively\n  serve   Serve the gallery over HTTP\n\nRun 'aurora-render <COMMAND> --help' for more information on a command.\n\nReport issues at the project tracker.\n",
    "root/version": "aurora-render 1.2.3\n",
    "render/usage": "usage: aurora-render render [OPTIONS] <SRC> [<DST>] [-- ARGS...]",
    "render/help": "Render one scene interactively\nusage: aurora-render render [OPTIONS] <SRC> [<DST>] [-- ARGS...]\n\nOptions:\n  -w, --watch            Re-render on change\n      --fps <FPS>        Target frame rate [range: 1, 240] [default: 60]\n      --format <FORMAT>  Leaf output format [possible values: png, webp] [default: png]\n\nHelp:\n  -h, --help  Show this help and exit\n\nArguments:\n  <SRC>  Source scene\n  <DST>  Target image\n\n",
    "strict/usage": "usage: strict [OPTIONS] <COMMAND> [-- ARGS...]",
    "strict/help": "A command that refuses to run bare\nusage: strict [OPTIONS] <COMMAND> [-- ARGS...]\n\nOptions:\n      --token <TOKEN>  Auth token [required]\n\nHelp:\n  -h, --help  Show this help and exit\n\nCommands:\n  deploy  Deploy the build\n\nRun 'strict <COMMAND> --help' for more information on a command.\n\n"
  },
